; The timetable of timetable.vae under the readings #solve selects. Cost vectors compare
; lexicographically, highest level first, so the bound [2 5] admits the two optima at
; [1 2] and every timetable at [2 2]: 15 in all. Ignoring the objective admits all 48
; timetables, and a limit of 3 takes three of them. The usc strategy reaches the two
; optima the default bb strategy does. Twin: timetable-readings.lp.
#base core
#include "timetable.vae"
#context CxTimetable
#solve {:among [2 5]}
#models (scheduledAt ?t ?s)
#solve {:among :all}
#models (scheduledAt ?t ?s)
#solve {:among :all :limit 3}
#models (scheduledAt ?t ?s)
#solve {:opt-strategy :usc}
#models (scheduledAt ?t ?s)
